            <ArticleTitle>[Pharma clinics. How I treat...or preventing pain with &quot;patches&quot;].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>586-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There exists two distinct types of patches aiming at increasing the pain threshold either systematically or locally. The first type of analgesic patch is a real transdermal delivery system releasing fentanyl. Such potent opioid drug exerts a systemic effect. The other type of patch associates lidocain and prilocain to induce a local anesthesia of the skin without inducing a systemic effect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
